  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "OTel Export for DSH",
      "text": "> DSH has cost dashboards, but no machine-readable export. This turns a `dsh-token-audit` JSON\n> summary into OTLP/JSON **metrics** for Grafana, Langfuse, or any collector that accepts JSON.\n\nIt is a **summary** exporter: cost, tokens, sessions, calls, projected monthly, idle/peak, and\nper-model totals. It does not produce per-turn or per-tool spans."
    },
    {
      "section": "Pipeline",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh-token-audit --all --format json > audit.json\nnode bin/dsh-otel.mjs --input audit.json --output otlp.json\n```\n\nIn DSH:\n\n```text\nUse otel_export on audit.json, format=summary.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Metrics",
      "text": "- `dsh.cost.cny`\n- `dsh.tokens.input`, `dsh.tokens.cache_read`, `dsh.tokens.output`\n- `dsh.sessions`, `dsh.calls`\n- `dsh.cost.projected_monthly_cny`\n- `dsh.cost.idle_cny`, `dsh.cost.peak_cny`\n- per model: `dsh.model.cost.cny`, `dsh.model.calls`, `dsh.model.tokens.output`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Boundaries",
      "text": "- No network: it writes JSON; your collector uploads it.\n- No per-turn/per-tool spans, no live streaming, no dashboard.\n- It inherits the audit's pricing; it does not re-price.\n- Redact the audit before exporting if titles/paths are sensitive.\n- OTLP/JSON only, not protobuf."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Provenance",
      "text": "Inspired by [claude-code-otel](https://github.com/ColeMurray/claude-code-otel); no source copied.\nSee `NOTICE.md`. License: MIT."
    }
  ],
